    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 4,
      "title": "Process vs. threads",
      "images": 14,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Process vs. threads",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.123,
          "bottom": 0.214,
          "x0": 226.0,
          "cw": 17.86
        },
        {
          "text": "• Parent P forks a child C",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.253,
          "bottom": 0.321,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 10.5
        },
        {
          "text": "– P and C do not share any memory",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.313,
          "bottom": 0.371,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 14.48
        },
        {
          "text": "– Need complicated IPC mechanisms to communicate",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.364,
          "bottom": 0.422,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 14.48
        },
        {
          "text": "– Extra copies of code, data in memory",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.415,
          "bottom": 0.473,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 14.48
        },
        {
          "text": "• Parent P executes two threads T1 and T2",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.465,
          "bottom": 0.533,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 10.5
        },
        {
          "text": "– T1 and T2 share parts of the address space",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.524,
          "bottom": 0.583,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 14.48
        },
        {
          "text": "– Global variables can be used for communication",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.575,
          "bottom": 0.634,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 14.48
        },
        {
          "text": "– Smaller memory footprint",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.626,
          "bottom": 0.685,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 14.48
        },
        {
          "text": "• Threads are like separate processes, except they",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.677,
          "bottom": 0.744,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 10.5
        },
        {
          "text": "share the same address space",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.729,
          "bottom": 0.792,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 12.96
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 5,
      "title": "Why threads?",
      "images": 14,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Why threads?",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.123,
          "bottom": 0.214,
          "x0": 272.1,
          "cw": 20.63
        },
        {
          "text": "• Parallelism: a single process can effectively utilize",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.243,
          "bottom": 0.311,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 10.5
        },
        {
          "text": "multiple CPU cores",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.296,
          "bottom": 0.358,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 12.78
        },
        {
          "text": "– Understand the difference between concurrency and",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.35,
          "bottom": 0.409,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 14.48
        },
        {
          "text": "parallelism",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.395,
          "bottom": 0.45,
          "x0": 137.8,
          "cw": 10.46
        },
        {
          "text": "– Concurrency: running multiple threads/processes at",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.442,
          "bottom": 0.501,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 14.48
        },
        {
          "text": "the same time, even on single CPU core, by",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.487,
          "bottom": 0.541,
          "x0": 137.8,
          "cw": 10.8
        },
        {
          "text": "interleaving their executions",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.528,
          "bottom": 0.582,
          "x0": 137.8,
          "cw": 10.32
        },
        {
          "text": "– Parallelism: running multiple threads/processes in",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.574,
          "bottom": 0.633,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 14.48
        },
        {
          "text": "parallel over different CPU cores",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.62,
          "bottom": 0.674,
          "x0": 137.8,
          "cw": 10.29
        },
        {
          "text": "• Even if no parallelism, concurrency of threads",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.665,
          "bottom": 0.733,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 10.5
        },
        {
          "text": "ensures effective use of CPU when one of the",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.718,
          "bottom": 0.78,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 12.52
        },
        {
          "text": "threads blocks (e.g., for I/O)",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.765,
          "bottom": 0.827,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 11.32
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 6,
      "title": "Scheduling threads",
      "images": 14,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Scheduling threads",
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 1,
          "para_break": true,
          "top": 0.123,
          "bottom": 0.214,
          "x0": 225.8,
          "cw": 18.88
        },
        {
          "text": "• OS schedules threads that are ready to run",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.206,
          "bottom": 0.267,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 9.45
        },
        {
          "text": "independently, much like processes",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.253,
          "bottom": 0.309,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 11.38
        },
        {
          "text": "• The context of a thread (PC, registers) is saved",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.301,
          "bottom": 0.362,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 9.45
        },
        {
          "text": "into/restored from thread control block (TCB)",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.348,
          "bottom": 0.405,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 11.01
        },
        {
          "text": "– Every PCB has one or more linked TCBs",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.397,
          "bottom": 0.451,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 13.34
        },
        {
          "text": "• Threads that are scheduled independently by kernel",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.444,
          "bottom": 0.505,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 9.45
        },
        {
          "text": "are called kernel threads",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.491,
          "bottom": 0.547,
          "x0": 106.2,
          "cw": 10.74
        },
        {
          "text": "– E.g., Linux pthreads are kernel threads",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.539,
          "bottom": 0.594,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 13.34
        },
        {
          "text": "• In contrast, some libraries provide user-level threads",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.586,
          "bottom": 0.647,
          "x0": 79.2,
          "cw": 9.45
        },
        {
          "text": "– User program sees multiple threads",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.639,
          "bottom": 0.694,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 13.34
        },
        {
          "text": "– Library multiplexes larger number of user threads over a",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.686,
          "bottom": 0.741,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 13.34
        },
        {
          "text": "smaller number of kernel threads",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.729,
          "bottom": 0.778,
          "x0": 137.8,
          "cw": 10.14
        },
        {
          "text": "– Low overhead of switching between user threads (no",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.771,
          "bottom": 0.825,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 13.34
        },
        {
          "text": "expensive context switch)",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.813,
          "bottom": 0.863,
          "x0": 137.8,
          "cw": 9.99
        },
        {
          "text": "– But multiple user threads cannot run in parallel",
          "kind": "text",
          "level": 0,
          "para_break": false,
          "top": 0.856,
          "bottom": 0.91,
          "x0": 115.2,
          "cw": 13.34
        }
      ]
    },
